t the plan does not enumerate them as edit targets.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff374ff5085c04f70","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Testing sections","norm_id":"n85f0cdfeb6a5a9b7","priority":0.7778,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Registering module_size_trend and cap_change_events makes test_cap_change_events_deregistered and test_a_real_spec_can_now_claim_the_freed_id fail during the test suite."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add these two tests to Scope, and either replace their negative assertions with positive registration/behavior assertions or delete them as superseded, noting the change in the plan.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the exact artifact and setting whose Git history yields cap_change_events (e.g. the config file path and cap key to diff across revisions), so the derivation source is unambiguous rather than 'Git-derived'.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1778,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'cap_change_events reports Git-derived module-cap changes with source and confidence metadata.'","Plan: 'Implement both metrics from Git history in the existing metrics subsystem.'","Code: existing Git metrics (churn, refactor_to_addition_ratio) derive only insertion/deletion sums from `git log --numstat` (_numstat_totals, git_metrics.py:96-142); the cap enters via ctx.size_cap (module_size_distribution, git_metrics.py:63-82), i.e. from configuration, not commit diffs.","ABSENCE: the plan does not name the config file/setting whose revision history yields cap-change events, so an implementer cannot know whether to diff a config file, replay events, or infer from numstat."],"finding":"The plan names 'Git-derived module-cap changes' for cap_change_events but does not specify WHICH artifact's history encodes the cap, so the core data-source mechanism is ambiguous. The configured cap is supplied via config (ctx.size_cap in git_metrics.py), not present in git log --numstat sums that churn/refactor_to_addition_ratio use; detecting a 'cap change' therefore requires tracking a specific config file/key across revisions, which the plan leaves unstated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff99b4cae18e87a92","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Acceptance Criteria (cap_change_events)","norm_id":"n7c24df651606e923","priority":0.7778,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer diffs the wrong artifact (e.g. attempts to derive cap changes from numstat, which never contains the cap) and produces meaningless or always-empty results.","Two plausible cap sources (packaged default vs project config override) disagree and the metric silently picks one."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cite